  // game-info's attack-id (:offset-assert 1144) field is declared uint32 and stays
  // declared uint32 (#122 R2: correctly-declared field, not a field edit) -- it is
  // genuinely used as a plain-array pointer at the three call sites below, proven from
  // game-info_ir2.asm: top-level-login lazily allocates (new 'global 'entity-perm-array
  // 64) into its slot, then methods 13/14/16 walk that pointer as a plain
  // (array entity-perm) (length at +0, elements at +12 stride 16, matching entity-perm's
  // own :size-assert and its aid field at +12 landing on +24 per element). This is the
  // decompiler's own pointer-type tracking gap, not a missing field, so the fix is
  // scoped to these ops, not the deftype. a0/gp is the register actually holding the
  // "this" pointer at each call's own load op (method 13's this arrives in a0 and is
  // never copied; methods 14/16 copy it to gp at op 0 first).
  "(method 13 game-info)": [[0, "a0", "game-info"]],
  "(method 14 game-info)": [[1, "gp", "game-info"]],
  "(method 16 game-info)": [[13, "gp", "game-info"]],
  // og:preserve-this task-counter's own offset-1168 load in (top-level-login game-info)
