  // resolved to game-info by that op (op 167 reads *game-info* directly, and every
  // intervening store through it decodes fine), yet register-type-cast entries at op 182
  // for gp, v1, or an intentionally-wrong sanity cast at op 0 for t9 (which should have
  // broken the very next op's jalr if casts were being read at all) all produced a
  // byte-for-byte identical error and log. That rules out "wrong register" or "wrong
  // type" and points at env.casts() not being consulted for this specific
  // FunctionKind::TOP_LEVEL_INIT function at all, a decompiler-internal gap rather than
  // a missing config idiom. Left unfixed; see the #122 R2 report for the full trail.
